-- 7. Standby — Lights off, one by one. The mains hum dies; insects, air, one
-- last glass note, the work song very low. The yard holds its breath; open coda.
-- ~40+ cycles (~114 s+ at 84 BPM; open-ended).
-- Leave the last chord and air ringing; `fadeSilence` and `hush` are separate
-- steps, evaluated in that order after the room has decayed.

glideBpm 84 16
-- the last machine stops; the room gets bigger
fadeSilence 16 [1,2,4,7,8,9]
d6 bassStand
xfadeIn 5 24 pianoCoda
-- the last low chord, very sparse
xfadeIn 4 32 $ slow 8 $ pianoPedal (slow 8 hStand)
d3 switchOff
xfadeIn 10 24 $ stack [air, windBed]

-- the mains hum dies
xfadeIn 3 32 mainsDown
-- a few insects in the dark
xfadeIn 9 32 $ degradeBy 0.7 insectChat
-- one last glass note from the canteen
xfadeIn 8 24 $ stack [motifGlass, bottleHoot]
-- a last, distant reed
xfadeIn 7 32 reedStand

-- the work song one more time, very low
xfadeIn 6 24 motifBass

-- leave the room ringing, then fade
fadeSilence 24 [3,4,5,6,7,8,10]

-- hush when the room has decayed
hush
